    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'is parameter depends the type of surface water model and whether or not the fixed\_con'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ductance option is specified.  If the fixed\_conductance option is specified, then the'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' hydraulic conductance is calculated as the product of bedleak and cfact.  In this cas'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'e, the conductance is fixed and does not change as a function of the calculated surfac'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'e water and groundwater head.  If the fixed\_conductance option is not specified, then'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' the definition of cfact depends on whether the surface water model represents one-dim'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ensional channel flow or two-dimensional overland flow.  If the surface water model re'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'presents one-dimensional channel flow, then cfact is the length of the channel cell in'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' the groundwater model cell.  If the surface water model represents two-dimensional ov'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'erland flow, then cfact is the intersection area of the overland flow cell and the und'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'erlying groundwater model cell. '
