    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 's in HWVA are the vertical area for flow.  Thus, values in the HWVA array contain dime'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'nsions of both length and area.  Entries in the HWVA array have a one-to-one correspon'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'dence with the connections specified in the JA array.  Likewise, there is a one-to-one'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' correspondence between entries in the HWVA array and entries in the IHC array, which '
