    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'll CONDEQN strings include: SPECIFIED--character keyword to indicate the multi-aquifer'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' well saturated conductance will be specified.  THIEM--character keyword to indicate t'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'he multi-aquifer well saturated conductance will be calculated using the Thiem equatio'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'n, which considers the cell top and bottom, aquifer hydraulic conductivity, and effect'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ive cell and well radius.  SKIN--character keyword to indicate that the multi-aquifer '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'well saturated conductance will be calculated using the cell top and bottom, aquifer a'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'nd screen hydraulic conductivity, and well and skin radius.  CUMULATIVE--character key'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'word to indicate that the multi-aquifer well saturated conductance will be calculated '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'using a combination of the Thiem and SKIN equations.  MEAN--character keyword to indic'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ate the multi-aquifer well saturated conductance will be calculated using the aquifer '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'and screen top and bottom, aquifer and screen hydraulic conductivity, and well and ski'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'n radius. The CUMULATIVE conductance equation is identical to the SKIN LOSSTYPE in the'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' Multi-Node Well (MNW2) package for MODFLOW-2005. The program will terminate with an e'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'rror condition if CONDEQN is SKIN or CUMULATIVE and the calculated saturated conductan'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ce is less than zero; if an error condition occurs, it is suggested that the THIEM or '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'MEAN conductance equations be used for these multi-aquifer wells.'
