    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'NATIVE\_CELL\_AVERAGING can be ``LOGARITHMIC'''', ``AMT-LMK'''', or ``AMT-HMK''''.  ``'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'AMT-LMK'''' signifies that the conductance will be calculated using arithmetic-mean th'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ickness and logarithmic-mean hydraulic conductivity.  ``AMT-HMK'''' signifies that the'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' conductance will be calculated using arithmetic-mean thickness and harmonic-mean hydr'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'aulic conductivity. If the user does not specify a value for ALTERNATIVE\_CELL\_AVERAG'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ING, then the harmonic-mean method will be used.  This option cannot be used if the XT'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') '3D option is invoked. The AMT-HMK ALTERNATIVE\_CELL\_AVERAGING option, in combination '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'with the DRY\_CELL\_SATURATION option, can be used to calculate the same horizontal co'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'nductance as MODFLOW-USG when upstream weighting is used (LAYCON=4).'
