    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' K33/K if the K33OVERK option is specified); for an unrotated case, this is the vertic'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'al hydraulic conductivity.  When anisotropy is applied, K33 corresponds to the K33 ten'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'sor component.  All included cells (IDOMAIN $>$ 0) must have a K33 value greater than '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'zero.'
