    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description is a rotation angle of the hydraulic conductivity tensor in degrees. The a'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ngle represents the third of three sequential rotations of the hydraulic conductivity '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ellipsoid. Following the rotations by ANGLE1 and ANGLE2 described above, ANGLE3 rotate'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 's the ellipsoid about its K11 axis. An array can be specified for ANGLE3 only if ANGLE'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') '1 and ANGLE2 are also specified. An array must be specified for ANGLE3 if ANGLE2 is sp'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ecified. A positive value of ANGLE3 represents clockwise rotation when viewed from any'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' point on the positive K11 axis, looking toward the center of the ellipsoid. A value o'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'f zero indicates that the K22 axis lies within the x - y plane.'
