    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description is a combination of the wetting threshold and a flag to indicate which nei'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ghboring cells can cause a cell to become wet. If WETDRY $<$ 0, only a cell below a dr'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'y cell can cause the cell to become wet. If WETDRY $>$ 0, the cell below a dry cell an'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'd horizontally adjacent cells can cause a cell to become wet. If WETDRY is 0, the cell'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' cannot be wetted. The absolute value of WETDRY is the wetting threshold. When the sum'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' of BOT and the absolute value of WETDRY at a dry cell is equaled or exceeded by the h'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ead at an adjacent cell, the cell is wetted.  WETDRY must be specified if ``REWET'''' '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'is specified in the OPTIONS block.  If ``REWET'''' is not specified in the options blo'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ck, then WETDRY can be entered, and memory will be allocated for it, even though it is'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' not used.'
