    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ions, and is used in conjunction with the value of FLOW value specified in the STRESS\'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') '_PERIOD\_DATA section. Available diversion options include:  (1) CPRIOR = `FRACTION'','
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' then the amount of the diversion is computed as a fraction of the streamflow leaving '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'reach IFNO ($Q_{DS}$); in this case, 0.0 $\le$ DIVFLOW $\le$ 1.0.  (2) CPRIOR = `EXCES'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'S'', a diversion is made only if $Q_{DS}$ for reach IFNO exceeds the value of DIVFLOW.'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' If this occurs, then the quantity of water diverted is the excess flow ($Q_{DS} -$ DI'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'VFLOW) and $Q_{DS}$ from reach IFNO is set equal to DIVFLOW. This represents a flood-c'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ontrol type of diversion, as described by Danskin and Hanson (2002). (3) CPRIOR = `THR'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ESHOLD'', then if $Q_{DS}$ in reach IFNO is less than the specified diversion flow DIV'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'FLOW, no water is diverted from reach IFNO. If $Q_{DS}$ in reach IFNO is greater than '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'or equal to DIVFLOW, DIVFLOW is diverted and $Q_{DS}$ is set to the remainder ($Q_{DS}'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' -$ DIVFLOW)). This approach assumes that once flow in the stream is sufficiently low,'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' diversions from the stream cease, and is the `priority'' algorithm that originally wa'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 's programmed into the STR1 Package (Prudic, 1989).  (4) CPRIOR = `UPTO'' -- if $Q_{DS}'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') '$ in reach IFNO is greater than or equal to the specified diversion flow DIVFLOW, $Q_{'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'DS}$ is reduced by DIVFLOW. If $Q_{DS}$ in reach IFNO is less than DIVFLOW, DIVFLOW is'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' set to $Q_{DS}$ and there will be no flow available for reaches connected to downstre'
