    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'reader readarray'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'longname connection lengths'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description is a symmetric array of size NJA.  For horizontal connections, entries in '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'HWVA are the horizontal width perpendicular to flow.  For vertical connections, entrie'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 's in HWVA are the vertical area for flow.  Thus, values in the HWVA array contain dime'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'nsions of both length and area.  Entries in the HWVA array have a one-to-one correspon'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'dence with the connections specified in the JA array.  Likewise, there is a one-to-one'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' correspondence between entries in the HWVA array and entries in the IHC array, which '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'specifies the connection type (horizontal or vertical).  Entries in the HWVA array mus'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 't be symmetric; the program will terminate with an error if the value for HWVA for an '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'n to m connection does not equal the value for HWVA for the corresponding n to m conne'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ction.'
