    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'longname source type'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description keyword indicating how concentration will be assigned for sources and sink'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 's.  Keyword must be specified as either AUX or AUXMIXED.  For both options the user mu'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'st provide an auxiliary variable in the corresponding flow package.  The auxiliary var'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'iable must have the same name as the AUXNAME value that follows.  If the AUX keyword i'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 's specified, then the auxiliary variable specified by the user will be assigned as the'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' concentration value for groundwater sources (flows with a positive sign).  For negati'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 've flow rates (sinks), groundwater will be withdrawn from the cell at the simulated co'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ncentration of the cell.  The AUXMIXED option provides an alternative method for how t'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'o determine the concentration of sinks.  If the cell concentration is larger than the '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'user-specified auxiliary concentration, then the concentration of groundwater withdraw'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'n from the cell will be assigned as the user-specified concentration.  Alternatively, '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'if the user-specified auxiliary concentration is larger than the cell concentration, t'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'hen groundwater will be withdrawn at the cell concentration.  Thus, the AUXMIXED optio'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'n is designed to work with the Evapotranspiration (EVT) and Recharge (RCH) Packages wh'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ere water may be withdrawn at a concentration that is less than the cell concentration'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') '.'
