    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'esents the maximum allowable residual between successive outer iterations at any singl'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'e model package element. An example of a model package that would use OUTER\_RCLOSEBND'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' to evaluate convergence is the SFR package which solves a continuity equation for eac'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'h reach.  The OUTER\_RCLOSEBND option is deprecated and has no effect on simulation re'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'sults as of version 6.1.1.  The keyword, OUTER\_RCLOSEBND can be still be specified fo'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'r backward compatibility with previous versions of MODFLOW 6 but eventually specificat'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ion of OUTER\_RCLOSEBND will cause MODFLOW 6 to terminate with an error.'
