    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'reader urword'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'optional true'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'longname print option'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description is an optional keyword that defines default non-linear and linear solver p'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'arameters.  SIMPLE - indicates that default solver input values will be defined that w'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ork well for nearly linear models. This would be used for models that do not include n'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'onlinear stress packages and models that are either confined or consist of a single un'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'confined layer that is thick enough to contain the water table within a single layer. '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'MODERATE - indicates that default solver input values will be defined that work well f'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'or moderately nonlinear models. This would be used for models that include nonlinear s'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'tress packages and models that consist of one or more unconfined layers. The MODERATE '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'option should be used when the SIMPLE option does not result in successful convergence'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') '.  COMPLEX - indicates that default solver input values will be defined that work well'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' for highly nonlinear models. This would be used for models that include nonlinear str'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ess packages and models that consist of one or more unconfined layers representing com'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'plex geology and surface-water/groundwater interaction. The COMPLEX option should be u'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'sed when the MODERATE option does not result in successful convergence.  Non-linear an'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'd linear solver parameters assigned using a specified complexity can be modified in th'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'e NONLINEAR and LINEAR blocks. If the COMPLEXITY option is not specified, NONLINEAR an'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'd LINEAR variables will be assigned the simple complexity values.'
