    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'longname no pseudo-transient continuation'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description is a flag that is used to disable pseudo-transient continuation (PTC). Opt'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ion only applies to steady-state stress periods for models using the Newton-Raphson fo'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'rmulation. For many problems, PTC can significantly improve convergence behavior for s'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'teady-state simulations, and for this reason it is active by default.  In some cases, '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'however, PTC can worsen the convergence behavior, especially when the initial conditio'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ns are similar to the solution.  When the initial conditions are similar to, or exactl'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'y the same as, the solution and convergence is slow, then the NO\_PTC FIRST option sho'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'uld be used to deactivate PTC for the first stress period.  The NO\_PTC ALL option sho'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'uld also be used in order to compare convergence behavior with other MODFLOW versions,'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' as PTC is only available in MODFLOW 6.'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') ''
