    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'type double precision'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'reader urword'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'optional true'
    write(output_unit, '(a)') 'longname fraction of outer maximum used with ats'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'description real value defining the fraction of the maximum allowable outer iterations'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' used with the Adaptive Time Step (ATS) capability if it is active.  If this value is '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'set to zero by the user, then this solution will have no effect on ATS behavior.  This'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' value must be greater than or equal to zero and less than or equal to 0.5 or the prog'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ram will terminate with an error.  If it is not specified by the user, then it is assi'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'gned a default value of one third.  When the number of outer iterations for this solut'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'ion is less than the product of this value and the maximum allowable outer iterations,'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') ' then ATS will increase the time step length by a factor of DTADJ in the ATS input fil'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'e.  When the number of outer iterations for this solution is greater than the maximum '
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'allowable outer iterations minus the product of this value and the maximum allowable o'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'uter iterations, then the ATS (if active) will decrease the time step length by a fact'
    write(output_unit, '(a)', advance='no') 'or of 1 / DTADJ.'
